Version 2.0.0: 2026-10-30    o Version 2.0.0 released.
                             o New bandwidth selector h.scv(): Smoothed
                               Cross-Validation (Hall, Marron & Park 1992) with
                               fully analytical closed-form criterion for the
                               Gaussian kernel.
                             o New logistic kernel K(x) = e^{-x}/(1+e^{-x})^2,
                               derivatives up to order 20 and exact constants
                               R(K^(r)), in all selectors, dkde(), kernel.fun()
                               and kernel.conv().
                             o New power kernel family Pow(s,t):
                               K(x) = c(1-|x|^s)^t on [-1,1], given as
                               kernel = "pow(s,t)" or kernel.pow(s, t), for any
                               s > 0, t >= 0, in all selectors, dkde(),
                               kernel.fun() and kernel.conv(). It reproduces
                               uniform, triangular, Epanechnikov, biweight,
                               triweight and tricube exactly.
                             o h.scv(): the SCV criterion is now correct for
                               derivatives (r > 0); the bias term uses the
                               (2r)-th derivatives of the normal convolutions
                               with sign (-1)^r (it was the r = 0 term).
                             o nthreads: 0 now always means all cores (capped
                               by OMP_THREAD_LIMIT) and a call no longer
                               changes the threads of later calls; h.ucv()
                               with 0 used a single thread. dkde() and h.mlcv()
                               now use nthreads. New Cpp_omp_threads().
                             o The five Marron & Wand (1992) samples kurtotic,
                               outlier, bimodal, trimodal and claw are now
                               documented (?"kedd-data"), lazily loaded and used
                               in examples, vignette and demos.
                             o GitHub repository https://github.com/ac-guidoum/kedd
                               (URL, BugReports, R-CMD-check workflow), CITATION
                               file, cheatsheet.
                             o plot() and lines() on a bandwidth object evaluate
                               the criterion at n.points = 100 bandwidths by
                               default (was 200): twice as fast.
                             o Added second author: Amel Henider.
Version 1.0.4: 2026-01-27    o Version 1.0.4 released.
